// The cathedral's front on the bailey: its great gate, three tiles wide, under a gable and between
// pinnacles, the great rose of moon-glass high in the roof's gable over it; traceried windows of
// moon-glass hung high either side, and a spire either side; statues of the Duchess's handmaids and
// silver trees before it.
â = moon_portal yaw=90 height=14 rose=17 on=n
à = moon_window rise=3.5 size=1.7
á = moon_spire height=20 on=%
ã = veiled_statue
ä = silver_tree
// The gorge's walls, seen across it from the Landing and down it from the Glass Bridge: tall houses
// built along the castle's wall top, hung out over the drop on their undercrofts; the city's towers
// among them (a clock stopped at midnight, a belfry, a lantern of moon-glass); great buttresses built
// down into the deep; oriels hung on the lower town's backs; and past the gorge's ends, and either side
// of the drop behind the cathedral, the rest of the city climbing away into the haze.
